# Package Signatures

All of the RPMs provided via the OpenHPC repository are signed with a GPG
signature. By default, the underlying package managers will verify these
signatures during installation to ensure that packages have not been altered.
The RPMs can also be manually verified and the public signing key fingerprint
for the latest repository is shown below:

`Fingerprint: 6E19 BE11 D9A0 82C0 0A7D B41A 7AC0 5F09 **40A90CC8**`

The following command can be used to verify an RPM once it has been downloaded
locally by confirming if the package is signed, and if so, indicating which key
was used to sign it. The example below highlights usage for a local copy of the
`ohpc-release` package and illustrates how the **key ID** matches the fingerprint
shown above.

```bash
rpm --checksig -v ohpc-release-3-1.el9.x86_64.rpm
ohpc-release-3-1.el9.x86_64.rpm:
    Header V3 RSA/SHA256 Signature, key ID 40a90cc8: OK
    Header SHA256 digest: OK
    Header SHA1 digest: OK
    Payload SHA256 digest: OK
    V3 RSA/SHA256 Signature, key ID 40a90cc8: OK
    MD5 digest: OK

```
